speechtext:
My hon. friend asks for a list. Well,
7.000	new jobs in Nova Scotia; 5,000 in New Brunswick;
16.000	in Quebec; 102,000 in Ontario-

Mr. Speaker, just before you move to Routine Proceedings, perhaps I can deal with a matter for which I think you will find there is unanimous consent.
There have been discussions among the parties with respect to the following order:
That, notwithstanding any Standing Orders, standing committees of the House be empowered to sit together in plenary session and in a series of joint sessions to hold a parliamentary forum on global climate change;
That the plenary session be held on Monday, April 23, 1990;
That, notwithstanding Standing Order 115, the joint sessions of standing committees be held during periods coinciding with the hours of sittings of the House;
That all questions relating to the organization of the forum and implementation of this order be decided by a committee composed of representatives chosen by participating committees, chaired by Dr. Harry Brightwell, MP;
That the organizational committee be empowered to print a single, joint record of the proceedings of the forum.
